# Read-only context inspection and fixed scan planning; no provider calls.
name: Inspect an immutable context diagram before selecting it for scans
size: 120x36
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY NO_COLOR
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 KUZUSHI_MODEL=openai-codex:gpt-5.5
require-shell: python3 @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/context_diagram.py @TMP_TARGET @ART seed
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | ready
submit: use sast
require-live-snap: 20 TOOLS | module
submit: options sast:scan
require-live-snap: 20 sast:scan | options
submit: set taskMode manual
submit: set tasks secret-scan
submit: scan batch
require-live-snap: 20 PLAN A STUDY | form
keys: Down Down Enter Up v
require-live-snap: 20 Inspect a context revision | inspect-first
ask: Does opening a diagram require inspection of the selected revision, with a clear next action and no new model work?
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 CONTEXT SUMMARY | preview
expect: Alpha
expect: v diagram
keys: v
require-live-snap: 20 CONTEXT DATA FLOW | diagram
expect: Alpha client
expect: Alpha receiver
expect: Alpha records
ask: Does the diagram identify the chosen revision and its grounding status, show concrete flows, and provide visible detail and return controls?
keys: Down Enter
require-live-snap: 15 Recorded input | linked-details
expect: reader.py:1
ask: Can the operator read the selected component's purpose and linked source evidence without leaving its context revision?
resize: 80x24
live-snap: details-80
ask: Are linked context and source evidence readable at 80x24 with useful navigation controls?
keys: Enter
resize: 60x20
live-snap: diagram-60
ask: Does the compact diagram preserve the selected component and make its full details reachable?
resize: 40x12
live-snap: diagram-40
ask: Does the smallest layout state its limits and preserve element navigation, details and return controls?
keys: Enter End
live-snap: details-40-last
expect: reader.py:1
ask: Is the complete evidence reachable at 40x12, without clipping the controls or implying a model action?
keys: Home Enter Down Down
resize: 96x89
live-snap: selected-flow-tall
ask: Does the tall layout make the selected flow and its trust boundary understandable?
keys: Down Down
resize: 160x48
live-snap: selected-boundary-wide
ask: Does the wide layout retain a comfortable reading width and show the selected boundary and crossing flow?
keys: Enter
live-snap: boundary-details
expect: Request boundary
expect: request
keys: Escape
require-live-snap: 15 CONTEXT SUMMARY | returned-context
ask: Does Back restore the same inspected context instead of choosing or activating another revision?
keys: v
require-live-snap: 15 TRUST BOUNDARY | reopened-details
ask: Does reopening the diagram preserve its selected element and detail mode?
keys: Escape
require-live-snap: 15 CONTEXT SUMMARY | leave-diagram
keys: a
require-live-snap: 20 Context selected for this study | context-selected
keys: L
require-live-snap: 30 Draft ready | selected-plan
require-shell: python3 @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/context_diagram.py @TMP_TARGET @ART selected
keys: Escape
require-live-snap: 15 OPTIONS | returned-options
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME NO_COLOR=1 KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 KUZUSHI_MODEL=openai-codex:gpt-5.5
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | restarted
paste-file: @ART/resume-command.txt
keys: Enter
nav-mode:
keys: a
require-live-snap: 20 PLAN A STUDY | recovered-study
keys: Down Down Enter Enter
require-live-snap: 25 CONTEXT SUMMARY | recovered-context
keys: v
require-live-snap: 20 CONTEXT DATA FLOW | recovered-diagram
expect: Alpha receiver
ask: Does a fresh no-color session display the study's saved context diagram, with the active workspace model unchanged and no jobs started?
require-shell: python3 @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/context_diagram.py @TMP_TARGET @ART resumed
keys: Escape Escape Escape C-c
